{"id": "EUVD-2026-103716", "enisaUuid": "cf52b0ea-cbaf-3fa1-af73-9dbd5bbec5c1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/cio: Fix NULL pointer dereference in ccw_device_get_util_str()\n\nThe channel path registry entry associated with a CHPID may be removed\nwhile the subchannel's PMCW still references that CHPID. In this case,\nchpid_to_chp() can return NULL, leading to a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nAdd the missing NULL check before dereferencing the returned pointer.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d8b21820caed9128945fffcedf03e2a4c21eee2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fc54e04dad90b15d0430118b3f288a1d64e66c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27e396a89f76f742abdbe9f8c4a58a6e806fdf59", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbf30e661ceb9a52c94c85719716391dcc29142a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e006ac90a4d331db1dd712b91fec849b45ffc01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3bbcb32deecc06ebb1762398399b566d5ff2fc9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44b16b02608058fc72198ac0205969f0f43065df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b76268dac968612f7283d59b539036de955b7d9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98476", "GHSA-cfjv-hvgg-mwp9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05dc9056-f30b-30e1-bff3-dac8b9f71337", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "199652309a4d6635fca19d7528d73ab9e219bd9a <dbf30e661ceb9a52c94c85719716391dcc29142a"}, {"id": "0bd398bd-b35e-3d36-a1a5-8d9e8a0b9073", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "32413400-e180-333e-97fa-ea417ba7eccc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "199652309a4d6635fca19d7528d73ab9e219bd9a <c3bbcb32deecc06ebb1762398399b566d5ff2fc9"}, {"id": "4439eb5b-81a0-39ea-8f93-a681538dae2d", "product": {"name": "Linux",